    "created_at": "2018-04-17T21:34:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-17T21:34:54Z",
    "body": "I strongly agree that, at minimum, giving a control over \"just display the alt as inline text\" vs \"show a box with some placeholder\" is important, and that it would be great to control the placeholder as well; tons of sites are doing this manually right now, so it's clearly an attractive cowpath for us to pave.\r\n\r\nAnd yeah, whatever we end up doing, it needs to work on both `img` and `source`.\r\n\r\nI would be remiss at this point if I didn't mention [FLIF](https://flif.info/); if we just implemented that (\"just\"), there'd be no need for a low-src, you can just display whatever prefix of the file you've downloaded so far.  (It even supports animation now! That's new and exciting!)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
