    "body": "I was thinking of using 'background', but as you point out it would need to be turned off when the image is loaded. Also, it wouldn't work right if there's padding on the image.\r\n\r\nAdding pseudo-classes for different states could help with styling, like https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:-moz-loading . That combined with 'background', or maybe 'content' if that should work for normal elements.",
